## Inspection findings
1. FIGURES ABSENT. 0 <figure> and 0 content <img> on every page, in every mode, including
   print. The ten Spec 008 figure carriers are MDX comments ({/* FIGURE[fig-U3-1]... */}) and
   emit no DOM at all, so neither the image nor the manifest alt text reaches the page or the
   accessibility tree. Prose nevertheless makes explicit deictic references to them
   ("the figure above", "the figure at the top of this topic", "the timeline at the top of
   this topic"): 2 on topic-01, 2 on topic-02, 2 on topic-03, 1 on topic-04, 1 on topic-05 by
   the driver's conservative regex; manual reading finds the same references plus
   topic-01's Activity instruction "Each group takes one of the three definitions from the
   figure at the top of this topic". Mitigation observed on reading: in every case the
   figure's instructional content is also stated in the surrounding prose, so meaning is
   recoverable; the references themselves are dangling.
2. MCQ OPTIONS HAVE NO STRUCTURE. Verified in the built DOM: each of the ten MCQs renders as a
   single <li><p> with options a)-d) concatenated inline, e.g. MCQ 1 renders as
   "...and which does it damage? (Understand) a) Best on observed practice; damages
   achievement gain b) Best on achievement gain; damages breadth ... d) It looks equally good
   on all three". No nested list, no <br>, no per-option element. Present on screen and in
   print. The same course's Unit 1 assessment authors options as "   - A) ..." and renders a
   proper nested <ul>, so this is a deviation from the established in-course pattern.
3. HEADING ORDER SOUND. Exactly one <h1> per page; h2/h3 nest correctly (topics: 9 h2 / 2-4 h3;
   assessment: 3 h2 / 6 h3). Right-hand table of contents reflects the real heading tree.
4. LINK TEXT SOUND. Zero links with "here" / "click here" / "link" / "read more" text on any
   inspected page.
5. NARROW VIEWPORT SOUND. No horizontal overflow at 360px on any page
   (scrollWidth == innerWidth == 360 everywhere). Breadcrumbs wrap, ToC collapses into an
   "On this page" disclosure, body text reflows without clipping.
6. A4 PRINT SOUND EXCEPT FOR 1 AND 2. Site chrome (navbar, sidebars, ToC) is correctly
   suppressed; content reflows to full page width; nothing is clipped at the right edge.
   The unit-assessment print view renders the question bank AND the "Answers and marking
   guidance" section in full, including all five ERQ rubric tables; no table is truncated.
   Saved A4 PDFs: topic-01-a4.pdf, unit-assessment-a4.pdf.

